        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Document mutable headers on Response.json()]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45665</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45665"/>
        <updated>2026-09-13T01:22:01.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229418842?u=7d062faa679963052685abcfb94895e5a17314c9&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Document that the headers on a response created by <code class="notranslate">Response.json()</code> are mutable, contrast them with the immutable headers on a fetched response, and demonstrate changing a header.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Readers currently have no indication that they can modify the headers after creating a JSON response.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">The Fetch Standard creates the response with a <code class="notranslate">response</code> headers guard. The proposed change for <code class="notranslate">Response.redirect()</code> is still pending in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5021076611" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/1944" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/fetch/pull/1944/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1944">whatwg/fetch#1944</a>, so this PR intentionally documents only the behavior that is already specified.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">Relates to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5249298581" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/858" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/mdn/issues/858/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/858">mdn/mdn#858</a>.</p>]]></content>
