    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF156 ClipBoard Async API - clarify types]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45620</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45620"/>
        <updated>2026-09-11T21:49:55.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF156 adds support for the async Clipboard API to use web custom formats.</p>
<p dir="auto">The  API allows you to create a <code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem</code> that contains several representations of a copied object, such as version in HTML and Text, and push it to the system clipboard. Something else can read the clipboard and get back tha object - then choose the best format it understands.</p>
<p dir="auto">The update allows you to (behind a pref) use other types than PNG, HTML, txt.</p>
<p dir="auto">What this update does is make the model above clear, because it wasn't - it referred too much to "arbitrary types" can didn't capture "different representations".</p>
<p dir="auto">This is the first part of the job. After this I'll do the custom web formats bit.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5312307167" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45430/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45430">#45430</a></p>]]></content>
